I finally got a chance to play with this a little.  The profusion of "-" 
is not quite as bad as I thought it would be, but it's not lovely.

It looks a bit funny after performing a magic mapping!

One problem: in tty, the corridor wall "-" is the same as a horizontal 
open door.

It's worth noting that since corridor walls, unlike room walls, don't 
differ in behavior depending on orientation, it's not so necessary 
to have different walls, except for aesthetics.
In tiles, I would actually prefer just to have a slightly different 
shade or color between "known stone" and "unexplored".  It's harder
to see how to do this in tty.

Finally, there should definitely be an option, a la lit_corridor, which
controls whether "known stone" and "unexplored" look different.  This 
way, one can play in tty without the clutter, and still have a way
to check what is and what isn't explored when it's useful.

